          "content": "# Agent persona\n\nFollow the task exactly.\n\n# Parent context\n\nThe following context supplements the delegated task. Follow the delegated task as written if this context conflicts with it.\n\nRun exactly `node wait.cjs` with your command tool and wait for it to finish. Then reply with exactly REPLAY_DONE. The test controls the command. Do not use any other tools.\n\n# Delegated task\n\nRun exactly `node wait.cjs` with your command tool and wait for it to finish. Then reply with exactly REPLAY_DONE. The test controls the command. Do not use any other tools.\n\n# Task completion\n\nTo return a step output, write .usine/outputs/<name>.json as { \"type\": \"your.type\", \"commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\", \"content\": <JSON value> }. Use a lowercase file-name slug (letters, digits, hyphens, or underscores) and a non-empty type of at most 128 characters. The commit is optional; when set, it must equal 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567, the pinned checkout base supplied by usine, even when HEAD resumes from salvage. Each file and its compact JSON content must be at most 8 MiB, with at most 10 outputs per attempt. Do not commit .usine/. Keep a child's outputs in place so usine can collect them after the parent returns.\n\nRun gates, tests, and CI watches in the foreground. If a tool starts background work, wait for its result and finish every dependent step before returning your final answer.\nDo not end a turn promising to resume after a background notification. Your final answer returns control to the caller and may end the Attempt and remove its worktree. Push all commits that must survive before returning.\nWhen the task configures a CI handoff, push the final head and return [usine:awaiting-ci] on its own line followed by the handoff JSON. Leave its completion labels for usine and relay a child handoff unchanged. The session ends and usine watches CI without an agent. Otherwise, a pending CI check remains unfinished work; wait for it before completing the task. For a genuine blocker, record it on the issue or pull request and report the incomplete work.\nFor an unresolved blocker, start your final answer with exactly [usine:blocked] on its own line, followed by the exact blocker and incomplete work. This reserved marker reports a failed Attempt. A child's report that starts with the marker fails the Attempt: return it verbatim as your own final answer. Use an ordinary final answer only after completing the task.\nWhen the work needs a decision that only the operator can make, post the question on the task's issue or pull request when it has one, then start your final answer with exactly [usine:question] on its own line, followed by the question and the options you see. This reserved marker ends the Attempt and asks the operator; usine does not run this task again on the same Item until the operator answers or the Item changes. Return a child's report that starts with this marker verbatim as your own final answer.\n\n# GitHub identity\n\nAll factory Agents use the same GitHub App identity, including the Agent that opened a pull request.\nSubmit pull request reviews with event COMMENT (gh pr review --comment), never APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES. Attach each review to the exact commit you reviewed.\nUse the Loop's outcome labels to report findings or a passed review, and remove the opposite outcome label. A passed label does not satisfy GitHub required approvals; the operator provides any independent approval and merges.\nAppend this signature to every GitHub comment, issue, pull request, or review you publish:\n— usine agent: developer"
